# Port from C — score is regression only

**Primary goal:** implement **C semantics** from `nethack-c/upstream/` (call order, flags, branches, RNG at each call site). **Secondary check:** `npm run score` confirms you did not break known anchors — it does **not** choose the next slice.

## Do

- Open the **C function** (e.g. `mklev.c` `fill_ordinary_room`, `mkobj.c`, `role.c`, `monmove.c` `dochug`) and port control flow into `js/`.
- **Delete** `fastforward.js` replay rows or `monmove.js` `_HARNESS` entries only when the **real** ported path consumes the same RNG sequence on the paths you exercised.
- Use a failing public session to **find which subsystem** to port next — then read C; do not paste session RNG into code.
- Run **`npm run score`** at **milestones** or when unsure — not after every single function (see [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-batch-workflow.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-batch-workflow.md)).
- Pick the next **batch** from [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-function-checklist.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-function-checklist.md) (one C file / call graph per commit).
- **Fast-verify** batches with `node tools/diag_rng_window.mjs` on a **locator** session before commit.

## Avoid (score-chasing)

- Adding **`fastforward.js`** draws because the log “expects” them without a matching call site in ported code.
- Tuning **`_HARNESS`** / `stepNum` hacks to move one index on one seed while logic stays stubby.
- Shallow stubs that log one draw (e.g. `mkobj` → only `rnd(2)` `next_ident`) where C runs a full chain — parity will diverge later even if a few indices match.
- Choosing work only because it might improve **1/44** without mapping to a C file and call graph.
- **Big-bang port:** landing the whole checklist then running score once — RNG drift is easier to localize with milestone checks.

## Fastforward / harness

- **`fastforward.js`** and moveloop harnesses are **scaffolding**, not the implementation. Growing them without porting C creates a second, session-shaped answer key.
- Prefer **strategic** C milestones: chargen (`wintty.c` / `role.c` / `u_init.c`), mklev fill + `mineralize` inside `makelevel`, real `fmon` + `dochug`, then peel harnesses.

## Session signals (locate work, not spec)

| Signal | Use for |
|--------|---------|
| `seed8000-tourist-starter` | Short startup / moveloop canary (OPTIONS fast path) |
| `seed0900`, `seed0006`, … | Chargen / tty menus (need real C pickers) |
| Any FAIL line | Which **phase** diverged — then **`rg` in upstream** |

